---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import Code from '@/components/Code.astro';
import { MotionEmphasisReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-emphasis.tsx';
import { MotionEmphasisAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-emphasis.ts';
import MotionEmphasisSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-emphasis.svelte';
import reactSource from '@/examples/react/motion-emphasis.tsx?raw';
import angularSource from '@/examples/angular/motion-emphasis.ts?raw';
import svelteSource from '@/examples/svelte/motion-emphasis.svelte?raw';
import { buttonClass, demoClass } from '@/components/motionDemo';
---
<MotionPage title="Motion: emphasis" description="Emphasis motions replay on each change of state, such as the press feedback of a button or a refused action.">
  <h1>Emphasis</h1>
  <p>An emphasis motion plays its keyframes forward each time an element's state changes: the press feedback of a button, or the shake that signals a refused action. The verb is <code>emphasize</code>, and the state is the <code>data-state</code> attribute.</p>

  <h2>Define</h2>
  <pre><code>{`import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

defineMotion('nudge', {
  verb: 'emphasize',
  keyframes: [{ scale: 1 }, { scale: 1.05 }, { scale: 1 }],
  timing: 'spring.fast.spatial',
});`}</code></pre>
  <p>The presets <code>press</code> (dips to 96 % and returns) and <code>shake</code> (shakes sideways by 6 px) are emphasis motions. The timing of <code>shake</code> is a linear 400 ms curve. The <code>spring.fast.spatial</code> spring overshoots by about 9.5 %: keep it for transforms of small pieces, as the README of the package recommends.</p>

  <h2>HTML</h2>
  <pre><code>{`<button type="button" data-motion="press" data-state="off">Press me</button>

// Each change of data-state replays the emphasis
button.dataset.state = 'on';

// Or from script, on the binding
getMotion(button, 'emphasis')?.play();`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>The press preset replays on each click, because the button changes its <code>data-state</code>. The shake replays on each click of its button.</p>
  <div class={demoClass}>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <button type="button" class={buttonClass} data-emphasis-press data-motion="press" data-state="0">Press me</button>
      <button type="button" class={buttonClass} data-emphasis-shake data-motion="shake" data-state="0">Refused action</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <pre><code>{`// Each click counts up the state of the button, which replays its emphasis
button.dataset.state = String(Number(button.dataset.state) + 1);`}</code></pre>

  <h2>In the frameworks</h2>
  <p>The state is the option that changes: React <code>useMotion('press', &#123; state &#125;)</code>, Angular <code>[udxMotionState]</code>, Svelte <code>&#123;&#64;attach motion('press', () =&gt; (&#123; state: count &#125;))&#125;</code>. Each change of the value replays the emphasis.</p>
  <Code codes={{ react: reactSource, angular: angularSource, svelte: svelteSource }}>
    <MotionEmphasisReact slot="react" client:only="react" />
    <MotionEmphasisAngular slot="angular" client:load />
    <MotionEmphasisSvelte slot="svelte" client:only="svelte" />
  </Code>

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, an emphasis is not animated: it applies its end frame.</p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>An emphasis has no presence: its element stays in the page.</li>
    <li>An emphasis restarts when it is interrupted by default. The <code>interrupt</code> option (<code>restart</code> or <code>carry</code>) is an option of the <code>emphasize</code> and <code>layout</code> verbs only.</li>
    <li>Use <code>play()</code> to replay it without changing the state.</li>
  </ul>

  <script>
    document.addEventListener('click', event => {
      if (!(event.target instanceof Element)) return;
      const press = event.target.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-emphasis-press]');
      if (press) press.dataset.state = press.dataset.state === 'on' ? 'off' : 'on';
      const shake = event.target.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-emphasis-shake]');
      if (shake) shake.dataset.state = String(Number(shake.dataset.state) + 1);
    });
  </script>
</MotionPage>
